<title>CHINA: China Jan-Feb sugar output up 21.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>China Jan-Feb sugar output up 21.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China produced 3.0806 million tonnes of sugar in the first two months of this year, up 21.6 percent from the same period of 1996, the State Statistical Bureau said on Thursday.</p>
<p>China produced 1.3446 million tonnes of sugar in February alone, the bureau said without giving a year-ago figure.</p>
<p>China's sugar crushing season is from October to April.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
